IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap3-logic`

-- SECTION 2016(h), ELECTRONIC BENEFIT TRANSFERS (7 U.S.C. 2016(h)): lines 976-1105 of usc07-ch51.txt. Subsections (a) to (g) are in snap3-s2016-a-to-g.l4, (i) to (k) in snap3-s2016-i-to-k.l4.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. A function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN (or MAYBE NUMBER, MAYBE DATE) with: JUST TRUE = the text says yes;
-- JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = the text does not say. A duty without a stated time is answered "has done": JUST TRUE if done, NOTHING if not.
-- Clocks: a deadline counted in hours (48 hours) is a number of hours and a deadline counted in days is a number of days; each regulative rule says which, because the unit of WITHIN is a convention of the file.
-- Source is a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text.

-- THE ACTS the regulative rules in paragraph (12) are about, and nothing else.
DECLARE `s 2016(h)(12) act` IS ONE OF
    `make the stored benefits available to the household`
    `provide sufficient notice to the household that benefits will be expunged due to inactivity`

-- THE LAST DAY for each dated duty in this subsection, taken from the words.
-- src:979 | Not later than October 1, 2002
@ref s 2016(h)(1)(A) the last day for implementing an electronic benefit transfer system (src:979)
`s 2016(h)(1)(A) the last day for implementing an electronic benefit transfer system` MEANS Date 1 10 2002

-- src:1101 | not later than January 1, 2021.
@ref s 2016(h)(14)(B)(iv) the last day for approving the demonstration projects (src:1101)
`s 2016(h)(14)(B)(iv) the last day for approving the demonstration projects` MEANS Date 1 1 2021

-- src:1104 | by not later than January 1, 2022
@ref s 2016(h)(14)(C)(i) the last day for authorizing implementation in all States (src:1104)
`s 2016(h)(14)(C)(i) the last day for authorizing implementation in all States` MEANS Date 1 1 2022

-- Effective through fiscal year 2023. A Federal fiscal year runs from 1 October to 30 September (NOTES.md, fork F-2016-4).
-- src:1078 | Effective through fiscal year 2023
@ref s 2016(h)(13)(B) the last day of fiscal year 2023 (src:1078)
`s 2016(h)(13)(B) the last day of fiscal year 2023` MEANS Date 30 9 2023

§ `s 2016(h) -- electronic benefit transfers`

§§ `s 2016(h)(1) State agency implementation of an electronic benefit transfer system`

-- src:977 | (1) In general.—
-- src:978 | (A) Implementation.—
-- src:979 | Not later than October 1, 2002, each State agency shall implement an electronic benefit transfer system under which household benefits determined under section 2017(a) or 2035 of this title are issued from and stored in a central databank, unless the Secretary provides a waiver for a State agency that faces unusual barriers to implementing an electronic benefit transfer system.
@ref s 2016(h)(1)(A) each State agency implements an electronic benefit transfer system by 1 October 2002 unless the Secretary waives (src:977-979)
-- In plain words: by 1 October 2002 each State agency must run a system that issues household benefits from, and stores them in, a central databank, unless the Secretary has granted that State agency a waiver for unusual barriers to implementing one.
GIVEN `the Secretary provides a waiver for the State agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the State agency implemented the system` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(1)(A) the State agency has met the duty to implement an electronic benefit transfer system in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary provides a waiver for the State agency` THEN
            CONSIDER `the date on which the State agency implemented the system`
                WHEN JUST implemented THEN
                    IF Day implemented AT MOST Day `s 2016(h)(1)(A) the last day for implementing an electronic benefit transfer system`
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    ELSE
                        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the Secretary provides a waiver for a State agency that faces unusual barriers to implementing an electronic benefit transfer system"
                        -- note (a State agency with a waiver that implemented after the date is not said to have met the duty; the duty does not apply to it, and the text sets no other date for it)
                        NOTHING
                WHEN NOTHING THEN
                    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the Secretary provides a waiver for a State agency that faces unusual barriers to implementing an electronic benefit transfer system"
                    -- note (the duty does not apply to a State agency with a waiver, and the text sets no other date for it)
                    NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the date on which the State agency implemented the system`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN
                    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no implementation date was supplied, and the question of whether the State agency has implemented the system yet depends on today's date, which the text does not give
                    NOTHING
                WHEN JUST implemented THEN
                    IF Day implemented AT MOST Day `s 2016(h)(1)(A) the last day for implementing an electronic benefit transfer system`
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    ELSE
                        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than October 1, 2002, each State agency shall implement an electronic benefit transfer system"
                        JUST FALSE

-- src:980 | (B) Timely implementation.—
-- src:981 | Each State agency is encouraged to implement an electronic benefit transfer system under subparagraph (A) as soon as practicable.
@ref s 2016(h)(1)(B) a State agency is encouraged to implement the system as soon as practicable (src:980-981)
-- In plain words: the text only encourages each State agency to implement the system sooner than the date in (A); it does not require it and does not forbid it, so the question "must it?" has no answer in the text.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(1)(B) the State agency is required to implement the system as soon as practicable` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Each State agency is encouraged to implement an electronic benefit transfer system under subparagraph (A) as soon as practicable" creates no duty, permission or power (NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
    NOTHING

-- src:982 | (C) State flexibility.—
-- src:983 | Subject to paragraph (2), a State agency may procure and implement an electronic benefit transfer system under the terms, conditions, and design that the State agency considers appropriate.
@ref s 2016(h)(1)(C) a State agency may procure and implement a system under the terms, conditions and design it considers appropriate, subject to paragraph (2) (src:982-983)
GIVEN `the system meets the standards in the Secretary's final regulations under paragraph (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(1)(C) the State agency may procure and implement the system under the terms, conditions, and design that it considers appropriate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the system meets the standards in the Secretary's final regulations under paragraph (2)`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to paragraph (2), a State agency may procure and implement an electronic benefit transfer system"
            -- note (a failed condition; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
            JUST FALSE

-- src:984 | (D) Operation.—
-- src:985 | An electronic benefit transfer system should take into account generally accepted standard operating rules based on—
-- src:986 | (i) commercial electronic funds transfer technology;
-- src:987 | (ii) the need to permit interstate operation and law enforcement monitoring; and
-- src:988 | (iii) the need to permit monitoring and investigations by authorized law enforcement agencies.
@ref s 2016(h)(1)(D) an electronic benefit transfer system should take into account generally accepted standard operating rules (src:984-988)
-- In plain words: the text says a system "should" take into account the standard operating rules listed in clauses (i) to (iii); it does not say it must, and does not say it need not, so the question "must it?" has no answer in the text.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(1)(D) the electronic benefit transfer system is required to take into account the standard operating rules` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "An electronic benefit transfer system should take into account generally accepted standard operating rules" creates no duty, permission or power (NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
    NOTHING

§§ `s 2016(h)(3) approval of a system in which participation is not optional`

-- src:1002 | (3) In the case of a system described in paragraph (1) in which participation is not optional for households, the Secretary shall not approve such a system unless—
-- src:1003 | (A) a sufficient number of eligible retail food stores, including those stores able to serve minority language populations, have agreed to participate in the system throughout the area in which it will operate to ensure that eligible households will not suffer a significant reduction in their choice of retail food stores or a significant increase in the cost of food or transportation to participating food stores; and
-- src:1004 | (B) any special equipment necessary to allow households to purchase food with the benefits issued under this chapter is operational at a sufficient number of registers to provide service that is comparable to service provided individuals who are not members of households receiving supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits, as determined by the Secretary.
@ref s 2016(h)(3) the Secretary does not approve a mandatory system unless enough stores participate and enough registers are equipped (src:1002-1004)
-- In plain words: where households have no choice but to take part, the Secretary must not approve the system unless (A) enough eligible retail food stores, including stores able to serve minority-language populations, have agreed to take part throughout the area so households are not much worse off in choice of stores, cost of food or transport,
-- and (B) the special equipment is working at enough registers to serve households comparably with other customers, as the Secretary determines.
GIVEN `participation in the system is not optional for households` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a sufficient number of eligible retail food stores have agreed to participate throughout the area` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any special equipment necessary is operational at a sufficient number of registers to provide comparable service, as determined by the Secretary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(3) the Secretary may approve the system` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `participation in the system is not optional for households` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a system described in paragraph (1) in which participation is not optional for households"
            NOTHING
        IF NOT `a sufficient number of eligible retail food stores have agreed to participate throughout the area` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Secretary shall not approve such a system unless— (A) a sufficient number of eligible retail food stores"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `any special equipment necessary is operational at a sufficient number of registers to provide comparable service, as determined by the Secretary` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(B) any special equipment necessary to allow households to purchase food with the benefits issued under this chapter is operational at a sufficient number of registers"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall not approve such a system unless"
            -- note (conditions that must be met, not conditions that oblige approval)
            NOTHING

§§ `s 2016(h)(4) to (6) costs, information and the Secretary's authority`

-- src:1005 | (4) Administrative costs incurred in connection with activities under this subsection shall be eligible for reimbursement in accordance with section 2025 of this title, subject to the limitations in section 2025(g) of this title.
@ref s 2016(h)(4) administrative costs of electronic benefit transfer activities are eligible for reimbursement under section 2025, within section 2025(g) (src:1005)
GIVEN `the cost was incurred in connection with activities under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2025(g) the cost is within the limitations in section 2025(g)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(4) the administrative cost is eligible for reimbursement in accordance with section 2025` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the cost was incurred in connection with activities under this subsection` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Administrative costs incurred in connection with activities under this subsection"
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE `s 2025(g) the cost is within the limitations in section 2025(g)`

-- src:1006 | (5) The Secretary shall periodically inform State agencies of the advantages of using electronic benefit systems to issue benefits in accordance with this subsection in lieu of issuing coupons to households.
@ref s 2016(h)(5) the Secretary periodically informs State agencies of the advantages of electronic benefit systems (src:1006)
GIVEN `the Secretary has informed State agencies of the advantages of using electronic benefit systems to issue benefits in lieu of issuing coupons to households` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(5) the Secretary has done what the paragraph requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary has informed State agencies of the advantages of using electronic benefit systems to issue benefits in lieu of issuing coupons to households` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says "periodically" and states no interval
            NOTHING

-- src:1007 | (6) This subsection shall not diminish the authority of the Secretary to conduct projects to test automated or electronic benefit delivery systems under section 2026(f) of this title.
@ref s 2016(h)(6) this subsection does not diminish the Secretary's authority to conduct projects under section 2026(f) (src:1007)
GIVEN `the project is one to test automated or electronic benefit delivery systems under section 2026(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(6) this subsection diminishes the authority of the Secretary to conduct the project` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the project is one to test automated or electronic benefit delivery systems under section 2026(f)` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection shall not diminish the authority of the Secretary to conduct projects to test automated or electronic benefit delivery systems under section 2026(f) of this title."
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "projects to test automated or electronic benefit delivery systems under section 2026(f)"
            NOTHING

§§ `s 2016(h)(8) replacement of cards`

-- src:1010 | (8) Replacement of cards.—
-- src:1011 | (A) Fees.—
-- src:1012 | A State agency may collect a charge for replacement of an electronic benefit transfer card by reducing the monthly allotment of the household receiving the replacement card.
@ref s 2016(h)(8)(A) a State agency may charge for a replacement card by reducing the household's monthly allotment (src:1010-1012)
GIVEN `the card is a replacement for an electronic benefit transfer card` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(8)(A) the State agency may collect a charge by reducing the monthly allotment of the household receiving the replacement card` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the card is a replacement for an electronic benefit transfer card` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "replacement of an electronic benefit transfer card"
            NOTHING

-- src:1013 | (B) Purposeful loss of cards.—
-- src:1014 | (i) In general.—
-- src:1015 | Subject to terms and conditions established by the Secretary in accordance with clause (ii), if a household makes excessive requests for replacement of the electronic benefit transfer card of the household, the Secretary may require a State agency to decline to issue a replacement card to the household unless the household, upon request of the State agency, provides an explanation for the loss of the card.
@ref s 2016(h)(8)(B)(i) the Secretary may require a State agency to decline a replacement card after excessive requests unless the household explains the loss (src:1013-1015)
-- In plain words: if a household asks for replacement cards excessively, the Secretary may require the State agency to refuse another one, unless the household, when the State agency asks, explains why the cards were lost.
-- This is subject to the terms and conditions of clause (ii).
GIVEN `the household makes excessive requests for replacement of its electronic benefit transfer card` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household, upon request of the State agency, provides an explanation for the loss of the card` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(8)(B)(i) the Secretary may require the State agency to decline to issue a replacement card to the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the household makes excessive requests for replacement of its electronic benefit transfer card` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a household makes excessive requests for replacement of the electronic benefit transfer card of the household"
            -- note (a failed "if"; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the household, upon request of the State agency, provides an explanation for the loss of the card` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the household, upon request of the State agency, provides an explanation for the loss of the card"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1016 | (ii) Requirements.—
-- src:1017 | The terms and conditions established by the Secretary shall provide that—
-- src:1018 | (I) the household be given the opportunity to provide the requested explanation and meet the requirements under this paragraph promptly;
-- src:1019 | (II) after an excessive number of lost cards, the head of the household shall be required to review program rights and responsibilities with State agency personnel authorized to make determinations under section 2014(a) of this title; and
-- src:1020 | (III) any action taken, including actions required under section 2015(b)(2) of this title, other than the withholding of the electronic benefit transfer card until an explanation described in subclause (I) is provided, shall be consistent with the due process protections under section 2015(b) or 2020(e)(10) of this title, as appropriate.
@ref s 2016(h)(8)(B)(ii) the Secretary's terms and conditions provide an opportunity to explain, a rights review after excessive losses, and due process (src:1016-1020)
-- In plain words: the Secretary's terms and conditions must (I) give the household the opportunity to give the explanation promptly, (II) require the head of the household to review program rights and responsibilities with State agency personnel after an excessive number of lost cards,
-- and (III) make any action other than withholding the card until the explanation is given consistent with the due process protections of section 2015(b) or 2020(e)(10).
GIVEN `the terms and conditions give the household the opportunity to provide the requested explanation and meet the requirements under this paragraph promptly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms and conditions require the head of the household, after an excessive number of lost cards, to review program rights and responsibilities with State agency personnel authorized to make determinations under section 2014(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any action taken other than withholding the card until the explanation is provided is consistent with the due process protections under section 2015(b) or 2020(e)(10)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(8)(B)(ii) the terms and conditions established by the Secretary provide what the clause requires` MEANS
    `snap3 every one of these holds` (LIST
        JUST `the terms and conditions give the household the opportunity to provide the requested explanation and meet the requirements under this paragraph promptly`
      , JUST `the terms and conditions require the head of the household, after an excessive number of lost cards, to review program rights and responsibilities with State agency personnel authorized to make determinations under section 2014(a)`
      , `any action taken other than withholding the card until the explanation is provided is consistent with the due process protections under section 2015(b) or 2020(e)(10)`
      )

-- src:1021 | (C) Protecting vulnerable persons.—
-- src:1022 | In implementing this paragraph, a State agency shall act to protect homeless persons, persons with disabilities, victims of crimes, and other vulnerable persons who lose electronic benefit transfer cards but are not intentionally committing fraud.
@ref s 2016(h)(8)(C) a State agency acts to protect homeless persons, persons with disabilities, victims of crimes and other vulnerable persons who lose cards but are not intentionally committing fraud (src:1021-1022)
-- In plain words: in carrying out paragraph (8) a State agency must act to protect vulnerable people who lose cards without intending fraud. The text names four groups, the last of them open ("other vulnerable persons"), so a person who is in none of the named groups is not thereby outside it.
GIVEN `the person is a homeless person, a person with a disability, a victim of a crime, or another vulnerable person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has lost an electronic benefit transfer card` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is intentionally committing fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(8)(C) the State agency must act to protect the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is intentionally committing fraud` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who lose electronic benefit transfer cards but are not intentionally committing fraud"
            JUST FALSE
        IF NOT `the person has lost an electronic benefit transfer card` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who lose electronic benefit transfer cards"
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the person is a homeless person, a person with a disability, a victim of a crime, or another vulnerable person`
                WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
                    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and other vulnerable persons who lose electronic benefit transfer cards"
                    -- note (the class ends in "other vulnerable persons", so being outside the three named groups does not put the person outside it)
                    NOTHING
                WHEN NOTHING THEN
                    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is vulnerable was not supplied
                    NOTHING

-- src:1021 | (C) Protecting vulnerable persons.—
-- src:1022 | In implementing this paragraph, a State agency shall act to protect homeless persons, persons with disabilities, victims of crimes, and other vulnerable persons who lose electronic benefit transfer cards but are not intentionally committing fraud.
@ref s 2016(h)(8)(C) the State agency has acted to protect the person (src:1021-1022)
GIVEN `the State agency has acted to protect homeless persons, persons with disabilities, victims of crimes, and other vulnerable persons who lose electronic benefit transfer cards but are not intentionally committing fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(8)(C) the State agency has done what the subparagraph requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency has acted to protect homeless persons, persons with disabilities, victims of crimes, and other vulnerable persons who lose electronic benefit transfer cards but are not intentionally committing fraud` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no time by which the State agency must act
            NOTHING

-- src:1023 | (D) Effect on eligibility.—
-- src:1024 | While a State may decline to issue an electronic benefits transfer card until a household satisfies the requirements under this paragraph, nothing in this paragraph shall be considered a denial of, or limitation on, the eligibility for benefits under section 2014 of this title.
@ref s 2016(h)(8)(D) declining to issue a card until the household meets the requirements is not a denial of or limit on eligibility (src:1023-1024)
GIVEN `the State agency declines to issue an electronic benefits transfer card until the household satisfies the requirements under this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(8) declining to issue the card is a denial of, or a limitation on, the eligibility for benefits under section 2014` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency declines to issue an electronic benefits transfer card until the household satisfies the requirements under this paragraph` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this paragraph shall be considered a denial of, or limitation on, the eligibility for benefits under section 2014 of this title"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "While a State may decline to issue an electronic benefits transfer card until a household satisfies the requirements under this paragraph"
            NOTHING

§§ `s 2016(h)(9) optional photographic identification`

