-- src:1040 | The term “electronic benefit transfer service” means the processing of electronic transfers of household benefits, determined under section 2017(a) or 2035 of this title, if the benefits are—
-- src:1041 | (I) issued from and stored in a central databank;
-- src:1042 | (II) electronically accessed by household members at the point of sale; and
-- src:1043 | (III) provided by a Federal or State government.
@ref s 2016(h)(11)(A)(iii) the meaning of "electronic benefit transfer service" (src:1040-1043)
-- In plain words: the processing of electronic transfers of household benefits worked out under section 2017(a) or 2035, if the benefits are issued from and stored in a central databank, electronically accessed by household members at the point of sale, and provided by a Federal or State government.
GIVEN `the service is the processing of electronic transfers of household benefits, determined under section 2017(a) or 2035` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits are issued from and stored in a central databank` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits are electronically accessed by household members at the point of sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits are provided by a Federal or State government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(11)(A)(iii) the service is an electronic benefit transfer service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the service is the processing of electronic transfers of household benefits, determined under section 2017(a) or 2035` AND `the benefits are issued from and stored in a central databank` AND `the benefits are electronically accessed by household members at the point of sale` AND `the benefits are provided by a Federal or State government` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The term “electronic benefit transfer service” means the processing of electronic transfers of household benefits, determined under section 2017(a) or 2035 of this title, if the benefits are"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1044 | (iv) Point-of-sale service.—
-- src:1045 | The term “point-of-sale service” means any product or service related to the electronic authorization and processing of payments for merchandise at a retail food store, including credit or debit card services, automated teller machines, point-of-sale terminals, or access to on-line systems.
@ref s 2016(h)(11)(A)(iv) the meaning of "point-of-sale service" (src:1044-1045)
GIVEN `the product or service is related to the electronic authorization and processing of payments for merchandise at a retail food store` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(11)(A)(iv) the product or service is a point-of-sale service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the product or service is related to the electronic authorization and processing of payments for merchandise at a retail food store` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any product or service related to the electronic authorization and processing of payments for merchandise at a retail food store"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1046 | (B) Restrictions.—
-- src:1047 | A company may not sell or provide electronic benefit transfer services, or fix or vary the consideration for electronic benefit transfer services, on the condition or requirement that the customer—
-- src:1048 | (i) obtain some additional point-of-sale service from the company or an affiliate of the company; or
-- src:1049 | (ii) not obtain some additional point-of-sale service from a competitor of the company or competitor of any affiliate of the company.
@ref s 2016(h)(11)(B) a company may not tie electronic benefit transfer services to another point-of-sale service (src:1046-1049)
-- In plain words: a company may not sell or provide EBT services, or set or vary their price, on the condition that the customer takes some additional point-of-sale service from the company or an affiliate, or does not take one from a competitor of the company or of an affiliate.
GIVEN `s 2016(h)(11)(A)(ii) the seller is a company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the sale or provision, or the consideration, is conditioned on the customer obtaining some additional point-of-sale service from the company or an affiliate of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sale or provision, or the consideration, is conditioned on the customer not obtaining some additional point-of-sale service from a competitor of the company or competitor of any affiliate of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(11)(B) the company may sell or provide electronic benefit transfer services, or fix or vary the consideration, on the condition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2016(h)(11)(A)(ii) the seller is a company` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (`the sale or provision, or the consideration, is conditioned on the customer obtaining some additional point-of-sale service from the company or an affiliate of the company` OR `the sale or provision, or the consideration, is conditioned on the customer not obtaining some additional point-of-sale service from a competitor of the company or competitor of any affiliate of the company`) THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company may not sell or provide electronic benefit transfer services, or fix or vary the consideration for electronic benefit transfer services, on the condition or requirement that the customer"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the condition or requirement that the customer— (i) obtain some additional point-of-sale service from the company or an affiliate of the company; or (ii) not obtain some additional point-of-sale service from a competitor"
            NOTHING

§§ `s 2016(h)(12) recovering electronic benefits`

-- src:1053 | (A) In general.—
-- src:1054 | A State agency shall establish a procedure for recovering electronic benefits from the account of a household due to inactivity, or due to the death of all members of the household.
@ref s 2016(h)(12)(A) a State agency establishes a procedure for recovering electronic benefits from the account of a household due to inactivity or the death of all its members (src:1053-1054)
GIVEN `the State agency has established a procedure for recovering electronic benefits from the account of a household due to inactivity, or due to the death of all members of the household` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(12)(A) the State agency has done what the subparagraph requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency has established a procedure for recovering electronic benefits from the account of a household due to inactivity, or due to the death of all members of the household` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no time by which the procedure must be established
            NOTHING

-- src:1055 | (B) Benefit storage.—
-- src:1056 | (i) In general.—
-- src:1057 | A State agency may store recovered electronic benefits off-line in accordance with clause (ii), if the household has not accessed the account after 3 months.
@ref s 2016(h)(12)(B)(i) a State agency may store recovered benefits off-line if the household has not accessed the account for 3 months (src:1055-1057)
-- "after 3 months" is read as "once 3 months have passed without access" (NOTES.md, fork F-2016-3). The storing must be in accordance with clause (ii).
GIVEN `the number of whole months the household has gone without accessing the account` IS A NUMBER
      `the State agency acts in accordance with clause (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(12)(B)(i) the State agency may store the recovered electronic benefits off-line` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of whole months the household has gone without accessing the account` LESS THAN 3 THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the household has not accessed the account after 3 months"
            -- note (a failed "if"; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
            JUST FALSE
        IF NOT `the State agency acts in accordance with clause (ii)` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A State agency may store recovered electronic benefits off-line in accordance with clause (ii)"
            -- note (a failed condition; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1058 | (ii) Notice of benefit storage.—
-- src:1059 | A State agency shall—
-- src:1060 | (I) send notice to a household the benefits of which are stored under clause (i); and
-- src:1061 | (II) not later than 48 hours after request by the household, make the stored benefits available to the household.
@ref s 2016(h)(12)(B)(ii)(I) the State agency sends notice to a household whose benefits are stored (src:1058-1061)
GIVEN `the State agency has sent notice to the household the benefits of which are stored under clause (i)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(12)(B)(ii)(I) the State agency has done what the subclause requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency has sent notice to the household the benefits of which are stored under clause (i)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no time by which the notice must be sent
            NOTHING

-- src:1058 | (ii) Notice of benefit storage.—
-- src:1059 | A State agency shall—
-- src:1060 | (I) send notice to a household the benefits of which are stored under clause (i); and
-- src:1061 | (II) not later than 48 hours after request by the household, make the stored benefits available to the household.
@ref s 2016(h)(12)(B)(ii)(II) the State agency makes stored benefits available not later than 48 hours after the household's request (src:1058-1061)
-- In plain words: when the household asks for stored benefits, the State agency has 48 hours to make them available. Forty-eight hours exactly is in time.
GIVEN `the number of hours between the request by the household and the moment the State agency makes the stored benefits available` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(12)(B)(ii)(II) the State agency made the stored benefits available in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of hours between the request by the household and the moment the State agency makes the stored benefits available` AT MOST 48 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than 48 hours after request by the household, make the stored benefits available to the household"
            JUST FALSE

-- THE DUTY AS A REGULATIVE RULE. The clock counts hours from the household's request; the State agency must make the stored benefits available within 48 of them.
-- src:1058 | (ii) Notice of benefit storage.—
-- src:1059 | A State agency shall—
-- src:1060 | (I) send notice to a household the benefits of which are stored under clause (i); and
-- src:1061 | (II) not later than 48 hours after request by the household, make the stored benefits available to the household.
@ref s 2016(h)(12)(B)(ii)(II) duty of the State agency to make stored benefits available within 48 hours of the request (src:1058-1061)
`s 2016(h)(12)(B)(ii)(II) duty to make the stored benefits available within 48 hours of the request` MEANS
    PARTY `the State agency`
    MUST `make the stored benefits available to the household`
    WITHIN 48
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the State agency` BECAUSE "the stored benefits were not made available to the household within 48 hours after the request"

-- src:1062 | (C) Benefit expunging.—
-- src:1063 | (i) In general.—
-- src:1064 | Subject to clause (ii), a State agency shall expunge benefits that have not been accessed by a household after a period of 9 months, or upon verification that all members of the household are deceased.
@ref s 2016(h)(12)(C)(i) a State agency expunges benefits not accessed for 9 months or on verification that all household members are deceased (src:1062-1064)
-- In plain words: after 9 months without access, or once it verifies that every member of the household has died, the State agency must expunge the benefits. The duty is subject to the notice rules of clause (ii).
-- "after a period of 9 months" is read as "once 9 months have passed without access" (NOTES.md, fork F-2016-3).
GIVEN `the number of whole months the household has gone without accessing the benefits` IS A NUMBER
      `the State agency has verified that all members of the household are deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency has given the notice that clause (ii) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(12)(C)(i) the State agency must expunge the benefits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of whole months the household has gone without accessing the benefits` LESS THAN 9 AND (NOT `the State agency has verified that all members of the household are deceased`) THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "benefits that have not been accessed by a household after a period of 9 months, or upon verification that all members of the household are deceased"
            NOTHING
        IF `the State agency has given the notice that clause (ii) requires` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to clause (ii)"
            -- note (clause (ii) qualifies the duty and the text does not say what follows if the notice is not given)
            NOTHING

-- THE LAST DAY for giving the notice: 30 days before the date on which the benefits are to be expunged.
-- src:1065 | (ii) Notice of benefit expunging.—
-- src:1066 | Not later than 30 days before benefits are to be expunged under clause (i), a State agency shall—
@ref s 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii) the last day for giving notice before expunging (src:1065-1066)
GIVEN `the date on which the benefits are to be expunged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii) the last day for giving notice before expunging` MEANS
    Date (Day `the date on which the benefits are to be expunged` MINUS 30)

-- src:1065 | (ii) Notice of benefit expunging.—
-- src:1066 | Not later than 30 days before benefits are to be expunged under clause (i), a State agency shall—
-- src:1067 | (I) provide sufficient notice to the household that benefits will be expunged due to inactivity, and the date upon which benefits will be expunged;
@ref s 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii)(I) the notice to the household is sufficient and given not later than 30 days before the expunging (src:1065-1067)
GIVEN `the notice says that benefits will be expunged due to inactivity and gives the date upon which benefits will be expunged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the benefits are to be expunged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii)(I) the State agency gave sufficient notice in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the notice says that benefits will be expunged due to inactivity and gives the date upon which benefits will be expunged` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provide sufficient notice to the household that benefits will be expunged due to inactivity, and the date upon which benefits will be expunged"
            JUST FALSE
        IF Day `the date on which the notice was given` AT MOST Day (`s 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii) the last day for giving notice before expunging` `the date on which the benefits are to be expunged`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than 30 days before benefits are to be expunged under clause (i), a State agency shall"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1065 | (ii) Notice of benefit expunging.—
-- src:1066 | Not later than 30 days before benefits are to be expunged under clause (i), a State agency shall—
-- src:1067 | (I) provide sufficient notice to the household that benefits will be expunged due to inactivity, and the date upon which benefits will be expunged;
-- src:1068 | (II) for benefits stored off-line in accordance with subparagraph (B), provide the household an opportunity to request that such benefits be restored to the household; and
@ref s 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii)(II) a household whose benefits were stored off-line has an opportunity to request restoration (src:1065-1068)
GIVEN `the benefits are stored off-line in accordance with subparagraph (B)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the household was given the opportunity to request that the benefits be restored` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the benefits are to be expunged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii)(II) the State agency gave the opportunity to request restoration in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the benefits are stored off-line in accordance with subparagraph (B)` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for benefits stored off-line in accordance with subparagraph (B)"
            NOTHING
        IF Day `the date on which the household was given the opportunity to request that the benefits be restored` AT MOST Day (`s 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii) the last day for giving notice before expunging` `the date on which the benefits are to be expunged`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than 30 days before benefits are to be expunged under clause (i), a State agency shall"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1065 | (ii) Notice of benefit expunging.—
-- src:1066 | Not later than 30 days before benefits are to be expunged under clause (i), a State agency shall—
-- src:1067 | (I) provide sufficient notice to the household that benefits will be expunged due to inactivity, and the date upon which benefits will be expunged;
-- src:1068 | (II) for benefits stored off-line in accordance with subparagraph (B), provide the household an opportunity to request that such benefits be restored to the household; and
-- src:1069 | (III) not later than 48 hours after request by the household, make the benefits available to the household.
@ref s 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii)(III) the State agency makes the benefits available not later than 48 hours after the household's request (src:1065-1069)
GIVEN `the number of hours between the request by the household and the moment the State agency makes the benefits available` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii)(III) the State agency made the benefits available in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of hours between the request by the household and the moment the State agency makes the benefits available` AT MOST 48 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than 48 hours after request by the household, make the benefits available to the household"
            JUST FALSE

-- THE NOTICE DUTY AS A REGULATIVE RULE. The clock counts days; the parameter is the number of days from the start of the clock to the last day for giving notice (the expunging date less 30).
-- src:1065 | (ii) Notice of benefit expunging.—
-- src:1066 | Not later than 30 days before benefits are to be expunged under clause (i), a State agency shall—
-- src:1067 | (I) provide sufficient notice to the household that benefits will be expunged due to inactivity, and the date upon which benefits will be expunged;
@ref s 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii)(I) duty of the State agency to give notice before the last day (src:1065-1067)
GIVEN `the number of days from the start of the clock to the last day for giving notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 2016(h)(12) act`
`s 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii)(I) duty to give sufficient notice before expunging` MEANS
    PARTY `the State agency`
    MUST `provide sufficient notice to the household that benefits will be expunged due to inactivity`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the start of the clock to the last day for giving notice`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the State agency` BECAUSE "sufficient notice that benefits will be expunged was not given by the last day, 30 days before the expunging"

-- src:1070 | (D) Notice.—
-- src:1071 | A State agency shall—
-- src:1072 | (i) send notice to a household the benefits of which are stored under subparagraph (B); and
-- src:1073 | (ii) not later than 48 hours after request by the household, make the stored benefits available to the household.
@ref s 2016(h)(12)(D) a State agency sends notice to a household whose benefits are stored, and makes them available within 48 hours of a request (src:1070-1073)
-- Subparagraph (D) repeats clause (B)(ii) in the words of the text; its two limbs are answered by the same tests.
GIVEN `the State agency has sent notice to the household the benefits of which are stored under subparagraph (B)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(12)(D)(i) the State agency has done what the clause requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency has sent notice to the household the benefits of which are stored under subparagraph (B)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no time by which the notice must be sent
            NOTHING

-- src:1070 | (D) Notice.—
-- src:1071 | A State agency shall—
-- src:1072 | (i) send notice to a household the benefits of which are stored under subparagraph (B); and
-- src:1073 | (ii) not later than 48 hours after request by the household, make the stored benefits available to the household.
@ref s 2016(h)(12)(D)(ii) the State agency makes the stored benefits available not later than 48 hours after the household's request (src:1070-1073)
GIVEN `the number of hours between the request by the household and the moment the State agency makes the stored benefits available` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(12)(D)(ii) the State agency made the stored benefits available in time` MEANS
