§§ `s 2016(h)(13) fees`

-- src:1074 | (13) Fees.—
-- src:1075 | (A) Interchange fees.—
-- src:1076 | No interchange fees shall apply to electronic benefit transfer transactions under this subsection.
@ref s 2016(h)(13)(A) no interchange fees apply to electronic benefit transfer transactions (src:1074-1076)
GIVEN `the transaction is an electronic benefit transfer transaction under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(13)(A) an interchange fee applies to the transaction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the transaction is an electronic benefit transfer transaction under this subsection` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No interchange fees shall apply to electronic benefit transfer transactions under this subsection."
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "electronic benefit transfer transactions under this subsection"
            NOTHING

-- src:1077 | (B) Other fees.—
-- src:1078 | Effective through fiscal year 2023, neither a State, nor any agent, contractor, or subcontractor of a State who facilitates the provision of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits in such State may impose a fee for switching (as defined in subsection (j)(1)(H)) or routing such benefits.
@ref s 2016(h)(13)(B) through fiscal year 2023 neither a State nor its agent, contractor or subcontractor may impose a fee for switching or routing benefits (src:1077-1078)
GIVEN `the date on which the fee is imposed` IS A DATE
      `the fee is for switching (as defined in subsection (j)(1)(H)) or routing supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person imposing the fee is a State, or an agent, contractor, or subcontractor of a State who facilitates the provision of the benefits in that State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(13)(B) the person may impose the fee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the fee is for switching (as defined in subsection (j)(1)(H)) or routing supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits`) OR (NOT `the person imposing the fee is a State, or an agent, contractor, or subcontractor of a State who facilitates the provision of the benefits in that State`) THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "neither a State, nor any agent, contractor, or subcontractor of a State who facilitates the provision of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits in such State may impose a fee for switching (as defined in subsection (j)(1)(H)) or routing such benefits"
            NOTHING
        IF Day `the date on which the fee is imposed` AT MOST Day `s 2016(h)(13)(B) the last day of fiscal year 2023` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Effective through fiscal year 2023, neither a State, nor any agent, contractor, or subcontractor of a State who facilitates the provision of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits in such State may impose a fee"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the bar is stated "through fiscal year 2023" and the text says nothing about later years
            NOTHING

§§ `s 2016(h)(14) mobile technologies`

-- src:1080 | (A) In general.—
-- src:1081 | Subject to subparagraph (B), the Secretary shall authorize the use of mobile technologies for the purpose of accessing supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits.
@ref s 2016(h)(14)(A) the Secretary authorizes the use of mobile technologies to access benefits (src:1080-1081)
GIVEN `the Secretary has authorized the use of mobile technologies for the purpose of accessing supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(14)(A) the Secretary has done what the subparagraph requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary has authorized the use of mobile technologies for the purpose of accessing supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the duty is "subject to subparagraph (B)", whose dates are encoded separately, and subparagraph (A) states no date of its own
            NOTHING

-- src:1083 | (i) Demonstration projects.—
-- src:1084 | Before authorizing implementation of subparagraph (A) in all States, the Secretary shall approve not more than 5 demonstration project proposals submitted by State agencies that will pilot the use of mobile technologies for supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits access.
@ref s 2016(h)(14)(B)(i) the Secretary approves not more than 5 demonstration project proposals before authorizing mobile access in all States (src:1083-1084)
GIVEN `the number of demonstration project proposals the Secretary has approved` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(14)(B)(i) the Secretary approved a number of proposals the clause allows` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of demonstration project proposals the Secretary has approved` AT MOST 5 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Secretary shall approve not more than 5 demonstration project proposals"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1085 | (ii) Project requirements.—
-- src:1086 | To be eligible to participate in a demonstration project under clause (i), a State agency shall submit to the Secretary for approval a plan that—
-- src:1087 | (I) provides recipient protections regarding privacy, ease of use, household access to benefits, and support similar to the protections provided under existing methods;
-- src:1088 | (II) ensures that all recipients, including those without access to mobile payment technology and those who shop across State borders, have a means of benefit access;
-- src:1089 | (III) requires retail food stores, unless exempt under section 2016(f)(2)(B) of this title, to bear the costs of acquiring and arranging for the implementation of point-of-sale equipment and supplies for the redemption of benefits that are accessed through mobile technologies;
-- src:1090 | (IV) requires that foods purchased with benefits issued under this section through mobile technologies are purchased at a price not higher than the price of the same food purchased by other methods used by the retail food store, as determined by the Secretary;
-- src:1091 | (V) ensures adequate documentation for each authorized transaction, adequate security measures to deter fraud, and adequate access to retail food stores that accept benefits accessed through mobile technologies, as determined by the Secretary;
-- src:1092 | (VI) provides for an evaluation of the demonstration project, including, but not limited to, an evaluation of household access to benefits;
-- src:1093 | (VII) requires that the State demonstration projects are voluntary for all retail food stores and that all recipients are able to use benefits in non-participating retail food stores; and
-- src:1094 | (VIII) meets other criteria as established by the Secretary.
@ref s 2016(h)(14)(B)(ii) a State agency's plan contains the protections and features the clause lists (src:1085-1094)
-- In plain words: to take part, a State agency's plan must (I) protect recipients as other methods do, (II) give every recipient a way to reach benefits, (III) make retail food stores that are not exempt bear the costs of equipment, (IV) keep prices no higher than by other methods,
-- (V) ensure documentation, security and access, (VI) provide for an evaluation, (VII) keep the projects voluntary for stores and let recipients use benefits in non-participating stores, and (VIII) meet the Secretary's other criteria.
GIVEN `the plan provides recipient protections regarding privacy, ease of use, household access to benefits, and support similar to the protections provided under existing methods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan ensures that all recipients, including those without access to mobile payment technology and those who shop across State borders, have a means of benefit access` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan requires retail food stores, unless exempt under section 2016(f)(2)(B), to bear the costs of acquiring and arranging for the implementation of point-of-sale equipment and supplies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan requires that foods purchased through mobile technologies are purchased at a price not higher than the price of the same food purchased by other methods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan ensures adequate documentation for each authorized transaction, adequate security measures to deter fraud, and adequate access to retail food stores, as determined by the Secretary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the plan provides for an evaluation of the demonstration project, including an evaluation of household access to benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan requires that the State demonstration projects are voluntary for all retail food stores and that all recipients are able to use benefits in non-participating retail food stores` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan meets other criteria as established by the Secretary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(14)(B)(ii) the plan contains what the clause requires` MEANS
    `snap3 every one of these holds` (LIST
        JUST `the plan provides recipient protections regarding privacy, ease of use, household access to benefits, and support similar to the protections provided under existing methods`
      , JUST `the plan ensures that all recipients, including those without access to mobile payment technology and those who shop across State borders, have a means of benefit access`
      , JUST `the plan requires retail food stores, unless exempt under section 2016(f)(2)(B), to bear the costs of acquiring and arranging for the implementation of point-of-sale equipment and supplies`
      , JUST `the plan requires that foods purchased through mobile technologies are purchased at a price not higher than the price of the same food purchased by other methods`
      , `the plan ensures adequate documentation for each authorized transaction, adequate security measures to deter fraud, and adequate access to retail food stores, as determined by the Secretary`
      , JUST `the plan provides for an evaluation of the demonstration project, including an evaluation of household access to benefits`
      , JUST `the plan requires that the State demonstration projects are voluntary for all retail food stores and that all recipients are able to use benefits in non-participating retail food stores`
      , `the plan meets other criteria as established by the Secretary`
      )

-- src:1095 | (iii) Priority.—
-- src:1096 | The Secretary may prioritize demonstration project proposals that would—
-- src:1097 | (I) reduce fraud;
-- src:1098 | (II) encourage positive nutritional outcomes; and
-- src:1099 | (III) meet such other criteria as determined by the Secretary.
@ref s 2016(h)(14)(B)(iii) the Secretary may prioritize proposals that would reduce fraud, encourage positive nutritional outcomes, or meet other criteria (src:1095-1099)
GIVEN `the proposal would reduce fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposal would encourage positive nutritional outcomes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposal would meet such other criteria as determined by the Secretary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(14)(B)(iii) the Secretary may prioritize the proposal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the proposal would reduce fraud` OR `the proposal would encourage positive nutritional outcomes` OR `the proposal would meet such other criteria as determined by the Secretary` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Secretary may prioritize demonstration project proposals that would"
            NOTHING

-- src:1100 | (iv) Date of project approval.—
-- src:1101 | The Secretary shall solicit and approve the qualifying demonstration projects required under subparagraph (B)(i) not later than January 1, 2021.
@ref s 2016(h)(14)(B)(iv) the Secretary approves the qualifying demonstration projects not later than 1 January 2021 (src:1100-1101)
GIVEN `the date on which the Secretary solicited and approved the qualifying demonstration projects` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(14)(B)(iv) the Secretary approved the demonstration projects in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the Secretary solicited and approved the qualifying demonstration projects`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no approval date was supplied, and whether the Secretary has approved the projects yet depends on today's date, which the text does not give
            NOTHING
        WHEN JUST approved THEN
            IF Day approved AT MOST Day `s 2016(h)(14)(B)(iv) the last day for approving the demonstration projects`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE
                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary shall solicit and approve the qualifying demonstration projects required under subparagraph (B)(i) not later than January 1, 2021."
                JUST FALSE

-- src:1102 | (C) Report to congress.—
-- src:1103 | The Secretary shall—
-- src:1104 | (i) by not later than January 1, 2022, authorize implementation of subparagraph (A) in all States, unless the Secretary makes a finding, based on the data provided under subparagraph (B), that implementation in all States requires further study by way of an extended pilot period or is not in the best interest of the supplemental nutrition assistance program; and
-- src:1105 | (ii) if the determination made in clause (i) is not to implement subparagraph (A) in all States, submit a report to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate that includes the basis of the finding.
@ref s 2016(h)(14)(C)(i) the Secretary authorizes mobile access in all States by 1 January 2022 unless the Secretary finds more study is needed or it is not in the program's best interest (src:1102-1105)
GIVEN `the Secretary makes a finding, based on the data provided under subparagraph (B), that implementation in all States requires further study by way of an extended pilot period or is not in the best interest of the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the Secretary authorized implementation of subparagraph (A) in all States` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(14)(C)(i) the Secretary authorized implementation in all States in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary makes a finding, based on the data provided under subparagraph (B), that implementation in all States requires further study by way of an extended pilot period or is not in the best interest of the supplemental nutrition assistance program` THEN
            CONSIDER `the date on which the Secretary authorized implementation of subparagraph (A) in all States`
                WHEN JUST authorized THEN
                    IF Day authorized AT MOST Day `s 2016(h)(14)(C)(i) the last day for authorizing implementation in all States`
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    ELSE
                        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the Secretary makes a finding, based on the data provided under subparagraph (B)"
                        -- note (with the finding the date does not bind, and the text sets no other date)
                        NOTHING
                WHEN NOTHING THEN
                    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the Secretary makes a finding, based on the data provided under subparagraph (B)"
                    -- note (with the finding the date does not bind, and the text sets no other date)
                    NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the date on which the Secretary authorized implementation of subparagraph (A) in all States`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN
                    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no authorization date was supplied, and whether the Secretary has authorized it yet depends on today's date, which the text does not give
                    NOTHING
                WHEN JUST authorized THEN
                    IF Day authorized AT MOST Day `s 2016(h)(14)(C)(i) the last day for authorizing implementation in all States`
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    ELSE
                        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by not later than January 1, 2022, authorize implementation of subparagraph (A) in all States"
                        JUST FALSE

-- src:1102 | (C) Report to congress.—
-- src:1103 | The Secretary shall—
-- src:1104 | (i) by not later than January 1, 2022, authorize implementation of subparagraph (A) in all States, unless the Secretary makes a finding, based on the data provided under subparagraph (B), that implementation in all States requires further study by way of an extended pilot period or is not in the best interest of the supplemental nutrition assistance program; and
-- src:1105 | (ii) if the determination made in clause (i) is not to implement subparagraph (A) in all States, submit a report to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate that includes the basis of the finding.
@ref s 2016(h)(14)(C)(ii) if the Secretary decides not to implement in all States, the Secretary reports the basis of the finding to the Committees (src:1102-1105)
GIVEN `the determination made in clause (i) is not to implement subparagraph (A) in all States` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has submitted to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report that includes the basis of the finding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h)(14)(C)(ii) the Secretary has done what the clause requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the determination made in clause (i) is not to implement subparagraph (A) in all States` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the determination made in clause (i) is not to implement subparagraph (A) in all States, submit a report"
            -- note (a failed "if"; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the Secretary has submitted to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report that includes the basis of the finding` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no time by which the report must be submitted
            NOTHING

§§ `s 2016(h) -- the answers section 2012 asks of this subsection (Group B of the seam register)`

-- Section 2012(i) asks whether a card was "issued under section 2016(h)" and section 2012(d) asks what an "electronic benefit transfer under section 2016(h)" is. The text of this subsection gives the description in paragraph (1)(A): benefits determined under section 2017(a) or 2035 are issued from and stored in a central databank.
-- src:977 | (1) In general.—
-- src:978 | (A) Implementation.—
-- src:979 | Not later than October 1, 2002, each State agency shall implement an electronic benefit transfer system under which household benefits determined under section 2017(a) or 2035 of this title are issued from and stored in a central databank, unless the Secretary provides a waiver for a State agency that faces unusual barriers to implementing an electronic benefit transfer system.
@ref s 2016(h) the card is issued under subsection (h) (src:977-979)
GIVEN `the household benefits are determined under section 2017(a) or 2035` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits are issued from and stored in a central databank under an electronic benefit transfer system of a State agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the card gives the household access to those benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2016(h) the card was issued under subsection (h)` MEANS
    `the household benefits are determined under section 2017(a) or 2035` AND `the benefits are issued from and stored in a central databank under an electronic benefit transfer system of a State agency` AND `the card gives the household access to those benefits`

-- src:977 | (1) In general.—
-- src:978 | (A) Implementation.—
-- src:979 | Not later than October 1, 2002, each State agency shall implement an electronic benefit transfer system under which household benefits determined under section 2017(a) or 2035 of this title are issued from and stored in a central databank, unless the Secretary provides a waiver for a State agency that faces unusual barriers to implementing an electronic benefit transfer system.
@ref s 2016(h) the form of the benefit is an electronic benefit transfer under section 2016(h) (src:977-979)
GIVEN `the household benefits are determined under section 2017(a) or 2035` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits are issued from and stored in a central databank under an electronic benefit transfer system of a State agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Form of benefit`
`s 2016(h) the form of the benefit when issued by electronic benefit transfer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household benefits are determined under section 2017(a) or 2035` AND `the benefits are issued from and stored in a central databank under an electronic benefit transfer system of a State agency` THEN JUST `an electronic benefit transfer under section 2016(h)`
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "household benefits determined under section 2017(a) or 2035 of this title are issued from and stored in a central databank"
            NOTHING
